  "Question": "In right triangle \\(ABC\\), \\(\\angle C=90^\\circ\\), \\(AC=3\\), and \\(AB=6\\). Find the measure of \\(\\angle A\\) in degrees.",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "60",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(\\cos A=AC/AB=3/6=1/2\\), so \\(\\angle A=60^\\circ\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Hypotenuse midpoint and an equilateral triangle\n\nLet \\(M\\) be the midpoint of hypotenuse \\(AB\\). The right-triangle median property makes \\(CM\\) equal to the known length \\(AC\\):\n\\[\nAM=CM=\\frac{AB}{2}=3=AC.\n\\]\nThus \\(\\triangle AMC\\) is equilateral, so \\(\\angle CAM=60^\\circ\\). Since \\(M\\) lies on segment \\(AB\\), \\(\\angle A=\\angle CAM=60^\\circ\\).",
